<!--
  Scheduled-post notice. Renders only on posts where `page.future?` is
  true (the post's date is later than `Time.now`). Like the draft banner,
  this only appears in development — production builds exclude future
  posts entirely unless ABQARI_INCLUDE_FUTURE=true is set.

  Why a banner: future-dated posts can sit in your repo for weeks. A
  visible reminder ("scheduled for…") prevents the surprise of "why is
  this post not appearing on prod yet?" — the answer is on the page.

  The displayed time always includes the timezone (`Z`/abbreviation)
  so the author sees Abqari's interpretation of their date string and
  can tell whether they wrote it in UTC, local, or with an explicit
  offset.
-->
<% if page.respond_to?(:future?) && page.future? && page.respond_to?(:date) && page.date %>
<aside class="future-banner" role="note" aria-label="Scheduled post notice">
  <p>
    <strong>Scheduled</strong> — this post will publish at
    <time datetime="<%= page.date.iso8601 %>"><%= page.date.strftime('%B %-d, %Y at %H:%M %Z') %></time>
    (<%= time_until(page.date) %>).
    Production builds skip future-dated posts; this preview only shows in development.
  </p>
</aside>
<% end %>
